WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.476
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Sarah. Welcome to Online A one, Book three.

2
00:00:06.776 --> 00:00:09.861
Hi! I'm Rithy. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.161 --> 00:00:17.980
Unit twenty-three: Everyday Heroes. In this unit, you will talk about people who help our community.

4
00:00:18.983 --> 00:00:19.868
Hero.

5
00:00:20.568 --> 00:00:23.427
Hero means a person who does brave or good things.

6
00:00:23.727 --> 00:00:25.343
My mum is my hero.

7
00:00:26.043 --> 00:00:28.916
Your turn. Say: Hero.

8
00:00:31.616 --> 00:00:32.385
Hero.

9
00:00:33.383 --> 00:00:34.442
Firefighter.

10
00:00:35.142 --> 00:00:38.524
Firefighter means a person whose job is to stop fires.

11
00:00:38.824 --> 00:00:41.032
The firefighter saved the cat.

12
00:00:41.732 --> 00:00:44.384
Your turn. Say: Firefighter.

13
00:00:47.084 --> 00:00:48.260
Firefighter.

14
00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:50.147
Nurse.

15
00:00:50.847 --> 00:00:53.659
Nurse means a person who looks after sick people.

16
00:00:53.959 --> 00:00:55.691
The nurse is very kind.

17
00:00:56.391 --> 00:00:59.195
Your turn. Say: Nurse.

18
00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:02.872
Nurse.

19
00:01:03.883 --> 00:01:04.629
Brave.

20
00:01:05.329 --> 00:01:07.723
Brave means not afraid of danger.

21
00:01:08.023 --> 00:01:09.640
Firefighters are brave.

22
00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:12.377
Your turn. Say: Brave.

23
00:01:15.077 --> 00:01:15.938
Brave.

24
00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:17.719
Save.

25
00:01:18.419 --> 00:01:21.185
Save means to help someone out of danger.

26
00:01:21.485 --> 00:01:23.078
Doctors save lives.

27
00:01:23.778 --> 00:01:25.966
Your turn. Say: Save.

28
00:01:28.666 --> 00:01:29.446
Save.

29
00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:31.080
Help.

30
00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:34.441
Help means to do something useful for someone.

31
00:01:34.741 --> 00:01:36.926
Police officers help people.

32
00:01:37.626 --> 00:01:40.557
Your turn. Say: Help.

33
00:01:43.257 --> 00:01:43.956
Help.

34
00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:45.963
Community.

35
00:01:46.663 --> 00:01:49.684
Community means the people who live in one area.

36
00:01:49.984 --> 00:01:51.624
We clean our community.

37
00:01:52.324 --> 00:01:54.674
Your turn. Say: Community.

38
00:01:57.374 --> 00:01:58.294
Community.

39
00:01:59.283 --> 00:02:00.064
Thank.

40
00:02:00.764 --> 00:02:02.589
Thank means to say thank you.

41
00:02:02.889 --> 00:02:04.529
Let's thank our heroes.

42
00:02:05.229 --> 00:02:07.916
Your turn. Say: Thank.

43
00:02:10.616 --> 00:02:11.350
Thank.

44
00:02:12.350 --> 00:02:14.466
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:14.766 --> 00:02:17.381
Rithy, who is a hero in your community?

46
00:02:18.683 --> 00:02:22.404
The firefighter is a hero. He saves people from fires.

47
00:02:23.717 --> 00:02:25.800
That's right. Who else?

48
00:02:27.117 --> 00:02:31.151
The nurse at the health centre. She helps sick people every day.

49
00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:33.730
How can we thank them?

50
00:02:35.017 --> 00:02:37.132
We can make cards and say thank you!

51
00:02:38.417 --> 00:02:42.134
Grammar focus: He and She helps  and saves .

52
00:02:42.434 --> 00:02:46.689
A firefighter saves people. A nurse helps sick people.

53
00:02:46.989 --> 00:02:52.472
With he, she or one person, add -s to the verb: he saves, she helps.

54
00:02:53.483 --> 00:02:56.263
Now read and listen. Heroes Near Us.

55
00:02:56.563 --> 00:02:58.575
Heroes are not only in films!

56
00:02:59.883 --> 00:03:03.555
A firefighter is brave and saves people from fires.

57
00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:07.662
A nurse helps sick people every day.

58
00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:12.796
A teacher helps children learn, and a farmer grows our food.

59
00:03:14.083 --> 00:03:16.420
We should thank the heroes in our community.

60
00:03:17.717 --> 00:03:20.346
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:20.646 --> 00:03:22.529
A nurse blank sick people.

62
00:03:22.829 --> 00:03:27.609
A, help. B, helps. C, helping.

63
00:03:31.617 --> 00:03:34.011
The answer is B: helps.

64
00:03:35.517 --> 00:03:37.621
Not afraid of danger means blank.

65
00:03:37.921 --> 00:03:41.295
A, brave. B, sick. C, quiet.

66
00:03:45.283 --> 00:03:47.550
The answer is A: brave.

67
00:03:49.050 --> 00:03:52.094
A person whose job is to stop fires is a blank.

68
00:03:52.394 --> 00:03:56.988
A, firefighter. B, nurse. C, farmer.

69
00:04:00.983 --> 00:04:03.587
The answer is A: firefighter.

70
00:04:05.083 --> 00:04:08.978
Now it's your turn to speak. Who is a hero in your community?

71
00:04:14.278 --> 00:04:19.647
My hero is the doctor in my village. She helps sick people, and she works very hard.

72
00:04:19.947 --> 00:04:21.587
Excellent answer, Rithy!

73
00:04:22.583 --> 00:04:28.045
Great work today! You learned eight new words and he and she helps  and saves .

74
00:04:28.345 --> 00:04:32.890
Today's value is gratitude. Say thank you for your home and family.

75
00:04:33.190 --> 00:04:36.202
See you in Unit twenty-four. Goodbye!

76
00:04:36.502 --> 00:04:39.456
Thank you, Ms. Sarah! Bye, everyone!

